# 🔥 Graphs (Part 1) - Introduction, Representation, BFS & DFS

## 📌 Introduction

A Graph is a non-linear data structure consisting of:

```text
Vertices (Nodes)
+
Edges (Connections)
```

Graphs are used to represent relationships between objects.

Examples:

```text
Social Networks
Google Maps
Computer Networks
Flight Routes
Web Pages
```

