# 4️⃣ Graph Representation

Two common methods:

```text
1. Adjacency Matrix
2. Adjacency List
```

---

# 5️⃣ Adjacency Matrix

Store graph in:

```text
2D Matrix
```

Example:

```text
1 -- 2
|    |
3 -- 4
```

Matrix:

```text
    1 2 3 4

1   0 1 1 0
2   1 0 0 1
3   1 0 0 1
4   0 1 1 0
```

---

## C++ Code

```cpp
int n = 4;

vector<vector<int>> adj(
    n + 1,
    vector<int>(n + 1, 0)
);

adj[1][2] = 1;
adj[2][1] = 1;

adj[1][3] = 1;
adj[3][1] = 1;
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Space: O(V²)
```

---

# 6️⃣ Adjacency List

Most commonly used representation.

Store neighbors of each node.

Example:

```text
1 → 2,3

2 → 1,4

3 → 1,4

4 → 2,3
```

---

## C++ Code

```cpp
int n = 4;

vector<int> adj[n + 1];

adj[1].push_back(2);
adj[2].push_back(1);

adj[1].push_back(3);
adj[3].push_back(1);
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Space: O(V + E)
```

Much better than matrix.

