# 7️⃣ Breadth First Search (BFS)

## 📖 Definition

BFS visits nodes:

```text
Level by Level
```

Uses:

```text
Queue
```

---

### Example

Graph:

```text
      1
     / \
    2   3
   / \
  4   5
```

BFS:

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

---

# 8️⃣ BFS Algorithm

```text
Push source node into queue

Mark visited

While queue not empty

    Remove front node

    Visit it

    Push all unvisited neighbors
```

---

## BFS Code

```cpp
void bfs(
    int start,
    vector<int> adj[],
    int n)
{
    vector<int> vis(
        n + 1,
        0
    );

    queue<int> q;

    q.push(start);

    vis[start] = 1;

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        int node = q.front();

        q.pop();

        cout << node << " ";

        for(int neighbor : adj[node])
        {
            if(!vis[neighbor])
            {
                vis[neighbor] = 1;

                q.push(neighbor);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

---

# 9️⃣ Depth First Search (DFS)

## 📖 Definition

DFS explores:

```text
As Deep As Possible
```

Uses:

```text
Recursion
```

or:

```text
Stack
```

---

### Example

Graph:

```text
      1
     / \
    2   3
   / \
  4   5
```

Possible DFS:

```text
1 2 4 5 3
```

---

# 🔟 DFS Algorithm

```text
Visit Node

Mark Visited

Visit all unvisited neighbors
```

---

## DFS Code

```cpp
void dfs(
    int node,
    vector<int> adj[],
    vector<int>& vis)
{
    vis[node] = 1;

    cout << node << " ";

    for(int neighbor : adj[node])
    {
        if(!vis[neighbor])
        {
            dfs(
                neighbor,
                adj,
                vis
            );
        }
    }
}
```

Calling:

```cpp
vector<int> vis(
    n + 1,
    0
);

dfs(1, adj, vis);
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ BFS vs DFS

| BFS | DFS |
|------|------|
| Queue | Stack / Recursion |
| Level Order | Depth First |
| Finds shortest path in unweighted graph | Does not guarantee shortest path |
| More memory | Less memory |
| O(V+E) | O(V+E) |

